==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|anti-|logarithm}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|mathematics}} The [[number]] of which a given number is the [[logarithm]] (to a given [[base]]). {{C|en|Functions}}
#: {{syn|en|antilog}}
#: {{ant|en|logarithm}}
#: {{ux|en|If ''x'' is the logarithm of ''y'', then ''y'' is the '''antilogarithm''' of ''x''.}}

